1593   0598                                    .ORG $0598
1594   0598             ; Table for the global level data, over game levels.
1595   0598             ; Bit0 - bit3 of $43B8 is the table index.
1596   0598             ; Data will be fetched two times. Once before and once after the 'spiral fill' animation.
1597   0598             ; The double call is really a side effect of always going through
1598   0598             ; `GameState = 2` on every level entry, including “levels” that are only the spiral transition.
1599   0598             ; So the first fetch is needless.
1600   0598             ; They did not special-case “skip global init until after spiral.”
1601   0598             ; $05A0 should be $CC but it was never fixed and has no side effect.
1602   0598             T0598:
1603   0598 A8 A8                              .DB T05A8 & $FF, T05A8 & $FF    ;init values for 1st alien wave (pointer to $05A8, $05A8)
1604   059A C0 C0                              .DB T05C0 & $FF, T05C0 & $FF    ;init values for 2st alien wave (pointer to $05C0, $05C0)
1605   059C A8 A8                              .DB T05A8 & $FF, T05A8 & $FF    ;init values for blue birds wave (pointer to $05A8, $05A8)
1606   059E A8 A8                              .DB T05A8 & $FF, T05A8 & $FF    ;init values for pink birds wave (pointer to $05A8, $05A8)
1607   05A0 B4 CC                              .DB T05B4 & $FF, T05CC & $FF    ;init values for mothership wave (pointer to $05B4, $05CC)
1608   05A2 B4 B4                              .DB T05B4 & $FF, T05B4 & $FF    ;init values for mothership wave (pointer to $05B4, $05B4)
1609   05A4 A8 A8                              .DB T05A8 & $FF, T05A8 & $FF    ;not used? pointer to $05A8, $05A8
1610   05A6 A8 A8                              .DB T05A8 & $FF, T05A8 & $FF    ;not used? pointer to $05A8, $05A8
1611   05A8             
